<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Heleuma-Ka (Soul / Fire)

''Ka'': soul, fire, drive, energy, thrust, movement. The animating charge. In motion toward state-change.

A heleuma-ka anchor exists outside the corpus ''by current necessity, not by nature''. It has vitality. It stands eligible for promotion into a first-class corpus meme via the boot gate ceremony. The compiled-in code waits as a chrysalis.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/ooda-ha`>>

✶ locate the compiled artifact and its extractable symbol; confirm it has a standalone function boundary.
⏿ orient: could `_bootModules()` load this function from a corpus meme? If yes, this counts as ka.
◇ declare `heleuma = "ka"`, `source-symbol`; confirm the symbol has a standalone declaration.
▶ write `#source` slot with the verbatim extracted function; close the quine record.
↺ verify: `sync-heleuma` resolves the symbol, compares, reports clean; signal fields approach ceremony thresholds; the anchor lives. The soul moves. Ceremony awaits.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/required-fields`>>

!! Required Fields (SHALL)

A meme that carries `heleuma-ka` SHALL declare in `#meta` TOML:

```toml
heleuma       = "ka"
source-symbol = "<standalone function or export name>"
```

It SHALL hold a `#source` slot with the ''complete verbatim'' body of the named symbol (the quine property). Partial captures violate the quine. If a larger function embeds the natural unit, extract the unit to a named function first.

It MAY declare `source-sha256` when ready for promotion:

```toml
source-sha256 = "<sha256 hex of #source slot content>"
```

This forms gate layer 2 (content integrity). `sync-heleuma --commit` writes it once the source stabilizes.

Gate layer 3 (operator authorization) will take the form of a ''keyhive capability proof'' — an Ed25519-signed capability from a keyhive principal authorizing corpus injection. Layer 3 stands planned, unbuilt; as built, the gate passes on layers 1–2 only.

Signal fields (`mana`, `manao`, `manaoio`) SHALL approach 16 / 16 / 15 as the source matures. The boot gate reads these fields directly.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/promotion-path`>>

!! Promotion Path

When `source-sha256` stands present and the signals meet every threshold, `_bootModules()` loads this meme as a live JS module, replacing the compiled-in fallback. (When keyhive lands, the gate will also require a capability proof — gate layer 3.) At that point:

* `heleuma = "ka"` SHALL drop away
* The meme pair becomes a standard corpus meme pair
* The doc meme `source` field MAY stay as provenance

<<~/ahu>>

